                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "FORTUNATELY I don't need to finish the game to know my review. \r\nFlashing lights + asinine 'aesthetic' restrictions are annoying enough, but they also hurt me. also some folks might want to be aware for more severe reasons e.g. seizures. Why they cared to list none of this on the game page but were self-involved enough to use the game description as game content is beyond me. Glad I didn't try to play this offline, or it would have simply appeared broken to me.\r\n\r\nforced fullscreen + no settings until you \"login\" with information in the game description + no settings to get rid of curve effect + VFX \"off\" still has vfx effect.\r\n\r\nI don't care why dev wanted to reproduce the headaches I got from the CRT days, but they did.\r\n\r\nsorry, don't care about how good your game is, you treat me as a user like doodoo, I review your game like doodoo.",
